# Title: HackTool - CrackMapExec PowerShell Obfuscation
# ID: 6f8b3439-a203-45dc-a88b-abf57ea15ccf
# Status: test
# Level: high
# Author: Thomas Patzke
# Date: 2020-05-22
# Tags: attack.execution, attack.stealth, attack.t1059.001, attack.t1027.005
# Description: The CrachMapExec pentesting framework implements a PowerShell obfuscation with some static strings detected by this rule.
# Converted by: Sigma Universal SIEM/EDR CLI

(((CommandLine CONTAIN "join*split" OR CommandLine CONTAIN "( $ShellId[1]+$ShellId[13]+'x')" OR CommandLine CONTAIN "( $PSHome[*]+$PSHOME[*]+" OR CommandLine CONTAIN "( $env:Public[13]+$env:Public[5]+'x')" OR CommandLine CONTAIN "( $env:ComSpec[4,*,25]-Join'')" OR CommandLine CONTAIN "[1,3]+'x'-Join'')")) AND (((Image="*\\powershell.exe" OR Image="*\\pwsh.exe")) OR ((OriginalFileName = "PowerShell.EXE" OR OriginalFileName = "pwsh.dll"))))
